From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 01:08:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] media3: AI DJ window transitions in
 CrossfadeExoPlayerAdapter (behind DjHooks, off by default)

Hooks only; all logic lives in :djAndroid.
- ctor param dj: DjHooks? (Koin getOrNull); with dj == null or DJ mode off every path is the original one
- 50 ms poll: keeps the (current, next) DJ context fresh, starts a prepared window when the outgoing SOURCE
  position reaches the plan's trigger, holds the plain crossfade back while a window is ready/running
- DjPlayerPort: window player = createExoPlayerInstance(), commit flips the queue (precached player parked at
  the takeover position, listener moved, session delegate = window), finish reuses finalizeCrossfade
- djAbortInternal() at every crossfade-cancel site (commit/seek/cleanup/load/release/cast) so pause, seek, skip,
  queue change and release during a window commit the incoming track at its mapped position
- with DJ on, the plain crossfade is the DJ fallback and uses DjSettings.fallbackCrossfadeMs
- media3 depends on :djAndroid; Media3ServiceModule loads djModule next to the media service module

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
